    {
      "id": 30,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -2500,
        350
      ],
      "size": [
        900,
        500
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 7,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "How to use this workflow",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Source video + audio inpaint experiment\n\n1. Upload a 24 fps source video with an audio track in **Load Video**. The source is trimmed to H3-compatible length, then its frames and audio are encoded as the latent to edit.\n2. Set independent video and audio start/end seconds in **INPAINT SOURCE VIDEO + AUDIO**. Defaults are 1–3 seconds because the included sample video is short. For a longer source, try 4–8 seconds.\n3. Start with audio strength 1.0 and video strength 0.25. Edit the prompt to request the desired speech/visual change.\n4. The final Save Video and separate MP3 both use the edited source audio. Outside the selected latent ranges, the source latent is restored exactly.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## MiniMax H3 per-row video inpainting\n\n1. Upload a **24 fps** source video containing an audio track.\n2. Upload or paint a mask image. **White regenerates; black preserves.** One mask image is broadcast across the full video.\n3. Edit the H3 prompt to describe the intended replacement inside the mask.\n4. Queue the workflow.\n\nThe **Trim Source AV** node drops trailing frames to the largest valid `17k+5` length and trims audio to the same 24 fps duration. Its `h3_length` output controls H3 conditioning.\n\nThe resized source frames feed all three spatial branches: video VAE encoding, the 32×32 grid preview, and any optional tracking. Replace the static Load Image mask connection with **SAM3 Track to Mask** for a moving temporal mask.\n\nThe source video is the main latent and must not also be connected as an H3 reference video. Use the MiniMax H3 video VAE for frames and the MiniMax H3 audio VAE for audio."
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
